    <p><span>Hi,
      </span><span>
      </span><span>I'm _SiCk</span></p>
    <p><span>(afflicted.sh, 0xdeadbeefnetwork on GitHub).</span></p>
    <p><span>=C2=A0The May 7 LWN
      </span><span>piece on "Dirty Frag" raises the question of how the
        bug surfaced
      </span><span>before Hyunwoo Kim's May 12 coordinated disclosure.</spa=
n></p>
    <p><span>=C2=A0At least one of
      </span><span>the public artifacts in circulation =E2=80=94 my "Copy F=
ail
        2: Electric
      </span><span>Boogaloo" repo =E2=80=94 is an n-day built from the publ=
ic
        netdev fix commit,
      </span><span>not a break from inside the embargo.=C2=A0</span><span><=
/span><span><br>
      </span></p>
    <p><span>Timeline on my end:
      </span><span>
      </span><span> - Steffen Klassert's fix landed publicly on
        netdev/net.git as
      </span><span> commit=C2=A0 f4c50a4034e62ab75f1d5cdd191dd5f9c77fdff4.
      </span><span>=C2=A0=C2=A0</span></p>
    <p><span>=C2=A0Brad Spengler (@spendergrsec) publicly called the commit
      </span><span> copyfail-class.
      </span><span> - I read the commit, recognized the xfrm ESP-in-UDP
      </span><span> MSG_SPLICE_PAGES no-COW path against shared pipe
        pages as an
      </span><span> LPE primitive, and built a PoC.=C2=A0</span></p>
    <p><span>- Published to GitHub and afflicted.sh on May 7.
      </span><span>
      </span><span>The repo credits Kim and Chen (discovery, upstream
        fix), Klassert
      </span><span>(maintainer fix), Spengler (public call-out), and
        Theori/Xint
      </span><span>(original Copy Fail, CVE-2026-31431) directly in the
        README.</span></p>
    <p><span>=C2=A0</span><span></span><span>I had no contact with anyone on
        the linux-distros embargo, no
      </span><span>awareness of the May 12 disclosure date, and no
        access to Kim's
      </span><span>write-up or PoC. The work is n-day weaponization from
        a public
      </span><span>upstream commit, which is standard practice once a
        security-relevant
      </span><span>fix lands in a public tree.
      </span><span>
      </span><span>Flagging this so parallel n-day work isn't
        characterized as a leak
      </span><span>from inside the coordinated process.</span></p>
    <p><span>=C2=A0Happy to confirm timeline
      </span><span>details if useful.</span></p>
    <p><span>Copy_Fail2-Electric_Boogaloo
      </span><span>Write-up:=C2=A0</span></p>
